       - Zeroed B
       - Did three nested loops t,r,s accumulating:
           B[r][s] += A[r][t] * A[s][t];

     We compute the same result more efficiently by:
       - Interpreting it as B = A * A^T
       - Exploiting symmetry: B[r][s] == B[s][r]
       - Computing dot products between *rows* of A so that the
         innermost loop walks contiguous memory.

     This preserves bitwise results because for each pair (r,s),
     both original and new code compute:
       sum_{t} A[r][t] * A[s][t]
     with the same left-associative accumulation order; we only
     avoid recomputing the symmetric counterpart. */
