       For each fixed (i,j), the sequence of arithmetic operations
       (subtractions over k = 0..i-1) is identical; we only change
       the loop ordering, improving data locality:

         - A[i][k] is loaded once per k and reused for many j.
         - A[k][j] is traversed with j as the inner index, i.e.,
           as contiguous row-wise accesses. */
    for (k = 0; k < i; ++k) {
      const DATA_TYPE Lik = Ai[k];
      const DATA_TYPE *restrict Ak = A_[k];

#if LUDCMP_BLOCK_SIZE > 0
      /* Block the j-loop for better cache reuse of row k and row i. */
